      "deviation": "The WebSocket context literal is typed as the class's public shape and asserted once: the core class has a private field a literal cannot carry (type-only). ACRYL's additions for plugin-owned upgrades (spec 047 T009): the context reports bufferedAmount; close() maps a code the protocol forbids on the wire to 1011 (application codes 1013, 4404 pass); the handler sees close exactly once; the option textOnly drops binary frames before onMessage; the option track hands each accepted socket to the mounting plugin's scope; a non-websocket Upgrade request is answered 400 when nothing else listens; setupWebSocket takes any emitter of upgrade events (UpgradeSource) instead of a Server, so the Host web server's exact-path upgrade routes can feed it. The two symbols that tie a handshake to its waiter are exported, for testWebSocket (src/test-websocket.ts, ACRYL's addition: an in-process client/server pair)."
